"end\" fill=\"currentColor\">-4</text><text x=\"128.0\" y=\"235.5\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\">-2</text><text x=\"128.0\" y=\"166.2\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\">2</text><text x=\"128.0\" y=\"131.5\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\">4</text><text x=\"128.0\" y=\"96.8\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\">6</text><text x=\"128.0\" y=\"62.2\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\">8</text><text x=\"128.0\" y=\"27.5\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\">10</text><text x=\"128.0\" y=\"209.3\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\">0</text><path d=\"M45.0 331.0L46.0 319.9L47.1 309.1L48.2 298.6L49.2 288.3L50.2 278.3L51.3 268.5L52.4 259.0L53.4 249.8L54.4 240.8L55.5 232.0L56.6 223.5L57.6 215.3L58.6 207.3L59.7 199.5L60.8 192.0L61.8 184.7L62.8 177.6L63.9 170.8L64.9 164.2L66.0 157.8L67.0 151.6L68.1 145.7L69.2 139.9L70.2 134.4L71.2 129.1L72.3 124.0L73.3 119.1L74.4 114.4L75.5 109.9L76.5 105.6L77.6 101.5L78.6 97.6L79.7 93.9L80.7 90.4L81.8 87.0L82.8 83.9L83.8 80.9L84.9 78.1L86.0 75.5L87.0 73.0L88.0 70.7L89.1 68.6L90.1 66.7L91.2 64.9L92.2 63.2L93.3 61.8L94.3 60.4L95.4 59.3L96.5 58.2L97.5 57.4L98.5 56.6L99.6 56.0L100.7 55.6L101.7 55.3L102.8 55.1L103.8 55.0L104.8 55.1L105.9 55.3L107.0 55.7L108.0 56.1L109.0 56.7L110.1 57.3L111.2 58.1L112.2 59.0L113.2 60.0L114.3 61.2L115.4 62.4L116.4 63.7L117.4 65.1L118.5 66.6L119.6 68.2L120.6 69.9L121.6 71.7L122.7 73.6L123.8 75.5L124.8 77.5L125.8 79.6L126.9 81.8L128.0 84.0L129.0 86.4L130.1 88.7L131.1 91.2L132.2 93.7L133.2 96.3L134.2 98.9L135.3 101.6L136.3 104.3L137.4 107.1L138.4 109.9L139.5 112.7L140.6 115.6L141.6 118.6L142.7 121.6L143.7 124.6L144.8 127.6L145.8 130.7L146.9 133.8L147.9 136.9L148.9 140.0L150.0 143.2L151.1 146.3L152.1 149.5L153.2 152.7L154.2 155.9L155.2 159.1L156.3 162.3L157.3 165.5L158.4 168.7L159.5 171.9L160.5 175.1L161.6 178.2L162.6 181.4L163.7 184.5L164.7 187.7L165.8 190.8L166.8 193.8L167.8 196.9L168.9 199.9L169.9 202.9L171.0 205.9L172.0 208.8L173.1 211.7L174.2 214.5L175.2 217.3L176.2 220.0L177.3 222.7L178.3 225.4L179.4 228.0L180.4 230.5L181.5 233.0L182.6 235.4L183.6 237.7L184.7 240.0L185.7 242.2L186.8 244.3L187.8 246.4L188.8 248.4L189.9 250.3L191.0 252.1L192.0 253.8L193.1 255.5L194.1 257.0L195.1 258.5L196.2 259.8L197.2 261.1L198.3 262.3L199.4 263.3L200.4 264.3L201.4 265.1L202.5 265.8L203.5 266.4L204.6 266.9L205.7 267.3L206.7 267.6L207.8 267.7L208.8 267.7L209.8 267.6L210.9 267.3L211.9 266.9L213.0 266.4L214.1 265.7L215.1 264.9L216.2 264.0L217.2 262.8L218.2 261.6L219.3 260.2L220.3 258.6L221.4 256.9L222.5 255.0L223.5 253.0L224.6 250.7L225.6 248.4L226.6 245.8L227.7 243.1L228.8 240.2L229.8 237.1L230.9 233.8L231.9 230.4L232.9 226.8L234.0 222.9L235.0 218.9L236.1 214.7L237.2 210.3L238.2 205.7L239.2 200.9L240.3 195.9L241.3 190.7L242.4 185.2L243.4 179.6L244.5 173.7L245.6 167.7L246.6 161.4L247.7 154.9L248.7 148.1L249.8 141.1L250.8 133.9L251.8 126.5L252.9 118.8L254.0 110.9L255.0 102.8L256.1 94.4L257.1 85.8L258.1 76.9L259.2 67.7L260.2 58.4L261.3 48.7L262.4 38.8L263.4 28.6\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"60.0\" cy=\"197.3\" r=\"3\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><circle cx=\"168.0\" cy=\"197.3\" r=\"3\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><circle cx=\"240.0\" cy=\"197.3\" r=\"3\" fill=\"currentColor\"/></svg>","options":[{"id":"A","label":"$f(x) = (x - 2)(x + 1)(x + 3)$"},{"id":"B","label":"$f(x) = -(x + 2)(x - 1)(x - 3)$"},{"id":"C","label":"$f(x) = (x - 2)(x - 1)(x - 3)$"},{"id":"D","label":"$f(x) = (x + 2)(x - 1)(x - 3)$"}]}'::jsonb,90,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"medium","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-017","answer_format":"mcq"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select '3149c6eb-4e46-26c5-b9d1-9684836e170c','{"option_id":"D"}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"A zero at $x = a$ corresponds to a factor $x - a$, so the zeros $-2$, 1, and 3 give the factors $x + 2$, $x - 1$, and $x - 3$. Also $(0 + 2)(0 - 1)(0 - 3) = 6$, which matches $f(0) = 6$. Choice A reverses every sign. Choice C reverses one sign. Choice B has the correct zeros, but $f(0)$ would be $-6$ and the graph would fall on the right."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='3149c6eb-4e46-26c5-b9d1-9684836e170c') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('14ebe48a-a35e-68b8-61ce-e526869fc1ab','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_spr','{"prompt":"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = a(x - 3)^2 + 5$, where $a$ is a constant. The graph of $y = f(x)$ in the xy-plane passes through the point $(5, 13)$. What is the value of $a$?"}'::jsonb,91,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"medium","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-018","answer_format":"spr"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select '14ebe48a-a35e-68b8-61ce-e526869fc1ab','{"accepted":["2"]}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"Substitute $(5, 13)$: $13 = a(5 - 3)^2 + 5 = 4a + 5$. So $4a = 8$ and $a = 2$."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='14ebe48a-a35e-68b8-61ce-e526869fc1ab') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('1649baa7-cc44-69a8-a107-37db6514a049','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_single_choice','{"prompt":"A ball is kicked upward, and its height, in feet, $t$ seconds after it is kicked is modeled by $h(t) = -16t^2 + 64t + 5$. What is the maximum height, in feet, that the ball reaches?","options":[{"id":"A","label":"$2$"},{"id":"B","label":"$5$"},{"id":"C","label":"$64$"},{"id":"D","label":"$69$"}]}'::jsonb,92,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"medium","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-019","answer_format":"mcq"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select '1649baa7-cc44-69a8-a107-37db6514a049','{"option_id":"D"}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"The maximum occurs at the vertex, $t = -\\frac{64}{2(-16)} = 2$ seconds, and $h(2) = -64 + 128 + 5 = 69$ feet. Choice A is the time of the maximum, not the height. Choice B is the starting height, $h(0)$. Choice C is the coefficient of $t$."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='1649baa7-cc44-69a8-a107-37db6514a049') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('5a05ec22-bd4e-6d24-fef2-1aa08e634c8b','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_single_choice','{"prompt":"The vertex of the graph of the quadratic function $y = f(x)$ is $(1, 4)$. The function $g$ is defined by $g(x) = f(x - 2) + 3$. What is the vertex of the graph of $y = g(x)$?","options":[{"id":"A","label":"$(3, 7)$"},{"id":"B","label":"$(3, 1)$"},{"id":"C","label":"$(-1, 7)$"},{"id":"D","label":"$(-1, 1)$"}]}'::jsonb,93,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"medium","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-020","answer_format":"mcq"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select '5a05ec22-bd4e-6d24-fef2-1aa08e634c8b','{"option_id":"A"}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"Replacing $x$ with $x - 2$ shifts the graph 2 units right, and adding 3 shifts it 3 units up. The vertex moves from $(1, 4)$ to $(1 + 2, 4 + 3) = (3, 7)$. Choice C shifts left instead of right. Choice B shifts down instead of up. Choice D makes both errors."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='5a05ec22-bd4e-6d24-fef2-1aa08e634c8b') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('c6c148fb-d1d8-eae1-6991-128e54004a6e','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_single_choice','{"prompt":"For a polynomial function $p$, $p(3) = 0$. Which of the following must be a factor of $p(x)$?","options":[{"id":"A","label":"$x + 3$"},{"id":"B","label":"$x - 3$"},{"id":"C","label":"$3x$"},{"id":"D","label":"$x^2 - 3$"}]}'::jsonb,94,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"medium","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-021","answer_format":"mcq"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select 'c6c148fb-d1d8-eae1-6991-128e54004a6e','{"option_id":"B"}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"By the factor theorem, $p(a) = 0$ exactly when $x - a$ is a factor of $p(x)$. With $a = 3$, $x - 3$ must be a factor. Choice A would mean $p(-3) = 0$. Choice C would mean $p(0) = 0$. Choice D would mean $p(\\sqrt{3}) = 0$ and $p(-\\sqrt{3}) = 0$; none of these is guaranteed."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='c6c148fb-d1d8-eae1-6991-128e54004a6e') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('2ca038ac-7d1f-f748-6054-659c13fb6de3','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_spr','{"prompt":"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = 3(x - 1)(x + 5)$. What is the x-coordinate of the vertex of the graph of $y = f(x)$ in the xy-plane?"}'::jsonb,95,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"medium","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-022","answer_format":"spr"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select '2ca038ac-7d1f-f748-6054-659c13fb6de3','{"accepted":["-2"]}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"The zeros of $f$ are 1 and $-5$. A parabola is symmetric about the vertical line through its vertex, which lies halfway between the zeros: $\\frac{1 + (-5)}{2} = -2$. The factor 3 stretches the graph but does not move the vertex horizontally."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='2ca038ac-7d1f-f748-6054-659c13fb6de3') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('a718b3fd-ca24-d33e-570e-69bffb1e3568','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_single_choice','{"prompt":"A radioactive substance has a half-life of 8 years, meaning the amount remaining is cut in half every 8 years. A sample contains 640 grams of the substance. How many grams will remain after 24 years?","options":[{"id":"A","label":"$80$"},{"id":"B","label":"$160$"},{"id":"C","label":"$\\frac{640}{3}$"},{"id":"D","label":"$320$"}]}'::jsonb,96,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"medium","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-023","answer_format":"mcq"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select 'a718b3fd-ca24-d33e-570e-69bffb1e3568','{"option_id":"A"}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"24 years is $\\frac{24}{8} = 3$ half-lives, so the amount is $640\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 80$ grams. Choice B uses only 2 half-lives and choice D uses only 1. Choice C divides by the number of half-lives instead of halving three times."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='a718b3fd-ca24-d33e-570e-69bffb1e3568') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('2408011a-b59b-e9f6-a4f0-9c979b5bf8ad','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_single_choice','{"prompt":"The table shows four values of $x$ and the corresponding values of $f(x)$ for a quadratic function $f$. Which equation defines $f$?","table":{"headers":["x","f(x)"],"rows":[["-1","6"],["0","1"],["1","-2"],["2","-3"]]},"options":[{"id":"A","label":"$f(x) = x^2 + 4x + 1$"},{"id":"B","label":"$f(x) = -x^2 - 2x + 1$"},{"id":"C","label":"$f(x) = x^2 - 4x + 1$"},{"id":"D","label":"$f(x) = x^2 - 5x + 1$"}]}'::jsonb,97,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"medium","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-024","answer_format":"mcq"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select '2408011a-b59b-e9f6-a4f0-9c979b5bf8ad','{"option_id":"C"}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"From $f(0) = 1$, the constant term is 1. Write $f(x) = ax^2 + bx + 1$. Then $f(1) = a + b + 1 = -2$ and $f(-1) = a - b + 1 = 6$. Adding gives $2a + 2 = 4$, so $a = 1$ and $b = -4$: $f(x) = x^2 - 4x + 1$. Check: $f(2) = 4 - 8 + 1 = -3$. Choice A has the wrong sign on $b$. Choice B fits $f(0)$ and $f(1)$ but not $f(-1)$ or $f(2)$. Choice D fits only $f(0)$."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='2408011a-b59b-e9f6-a4f0-9c979b5bf8ad') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('479e81b7-8067-aae4-6683-b3ed0cb0a16e','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_single_choice','{"prompt":"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = x^2 + 6x + c$, where $c$ is a constant. In the xy-plane, the vertex of the graph of $y = f(x)$ lies on the x-axis. What is the value of $c$?","options":[{"id":"A","label":"$3$"},{"id":"B","label":"$6$"},{"id":"C","label":"$9$"},{"id":"D","label":"$36$"}]}'::jsonb,98,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"medium","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-025","answer_format":"mcq"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select '479e81b7-8067-aae4-6683-b3ed0cb0a16e','{"option_id":"C"}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"The vertex is on the x-axis exactly when the minimum value of $f$ is 0, which means $f(x)$ is a perfect square: $x^2 + 6x + 9 = (x + 3)^2$. So $c = 9$. Choice A is half of the $x$-coefficient, before squaring. Choice B is the $x$-coefficient itself. Choice D is $6^2$, without dividing by 4."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='479e81b7-8067-aae4-6683-b3ed0cb0a16e') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('4927bbd8-2840-a4d0-7291-c3514ec543e4','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_single_choice','{"prompt":"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = x^2 - 2x - 24$. Which of the following equivalent forms of $f(x)$ displays the x-intercepts of the graph of $y = f(x)$ as constants or coefficients?","options":[{"id":"A","label":"$(x - 1)^2 - 25$"},{"id":"B","label":"$x(x - 2) - 24$"},{"id":"C","label":"$x^2 - 2(x + 12)$"},{"id":"D","label":"$(x - 6)(x + 4)$"}]}'::jsonb,99,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"medium","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-026","answer_format":"mcq"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select '4927bbd8-2840-a4d0-7291-c3514ec543e4','{"option_id":"D"}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"The factored form $(x - 6)(x + 4)$ shows that $f(x) = 0$ when $x = 6$ or $x = -4$, so the x-intercepts are $(6, 0)$ and $(-4, 0)$. Choice A is vertex form, which displays the vertex $(1, -25)$. Choice B and choice C are other rewritings that do not show where $f(x) = 0$."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='4927bbd8-2840-a4d0-7291-c3514ec543e4') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('514cb047-10e2-f6cc-a8bf-c743b32d2758','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_single_choice','{"prompt":"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = 2^x - 8$. At what point does the graph of $y = f(x)$ cross the x-axis?","options":[{"id":"A","label":"$(3, 0)$"},{"id":"B","label":"$(4, 0)$"},{"id":"C","label":"$(0, 3)$"},{"id":"D","label":"$(0, -7)$"}]}'::jsonb,100,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"medium","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-027","answer_format":"mcq"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select '514cb047-10e2-f6cc-a8bf-c743b32d2758','{"option_id":"A"}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"The graph crosses the x-axis where $f(x) = 0$: $2^x = 8 = 2^3$, so $x = 3$, and the point is $(3, 0)$. Choice D is the y-intercept, since $f(0) = 1 - 8 = -7$. Choice B solves $2x = 8$, treating the exponent as multiplication. Choice C has the right number in the wrong coordinate."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='514cb047-10e2-f6cc-a8bf-c743b32d2758') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('0f95f9cf-f192-285c-68ef-19f074e0b298','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_spr','{"prompt":"The graph of the quadratic function $y = f(x)$ in the xy-plane has its vertex at $(3, -8)$ and passes through the point $(5, 0)$. What is the value of $f(0)$?"}'::jsonb,101,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"hard","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-028","answer_format":"spr"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select '0f95f9cf-f192-285c-68ef-19f074e0b298','{"accepted":["10"]}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"Use vertex form: $f(x) = a(x - 3)^2 - 8$. Since $f(5) = 0$, $4a - 8 = 0$ and $a = 2$. Then $f(0) = 2(0 - 3)^2 - 8 = 18 - 8 = 10$."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='0f95f9cf-f192-285c-68ef-19f074e0b298') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('ea6a2e3a-abe4-7a5b-21b3-603f88c8d408','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_single_choice','{"prompt":"A bacteria population is modeled by $N(t) = 400(1.5)^{\\frac{t}{2}}$, where $t$ is the time in hours. By what factor does the population increase every 6 hours?","options":[{"id":"A","label":"$2.25$"},{"id":"B","label":"$3.375$"},{"id":"C","label":"$4.5$"},{"id":"D","label":"$9$"}]}'::jsonb,102,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"hard","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-029","answer_format":"mcq"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select 'ea6a2e3a-abe4-7a5b-21b3-603f88c8d408','{"option_id":"B"}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"Increasing $t$ by 6 increases the exponent $\\frac{t}{2}$ by 3, so the population is multiplied by $1.5^3 = 3.375$. Choice A uses 2 periods instead of 3. Choice C multiplies 1.5 by 3 instead of raising it to the third power. Choice D multiplies 1.5 by 6."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='ea6a2e3a-abe4-7a5b-21b3-603f88c8d408') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.content_units(id,part_id,type,data,display_order,metadata) values('d5f99c7e-a748-b195-e335-5a871736086b','20dc549c-274c-938f-fb11-e72eb65b2a6e','question_single_choice','{"prompt":"The balance $B$, in dollars, in a savings account $t$ years after it is opened is modeled by $B(t) = 2{,}000(1.02)^{12t}$. Which of the following functions best approximates this model?","options":[{"id":"A","label":"$B(t) = 2{,}000(1.24)^t$"},{"id":"B","label":"$B(t) = 2{,}000(1.268)^t$"},{"id":"C","label":"$B(t) = 24{,}000(1.02)^t$"},{"id":"D","label":"$B(t) = 2{,}000(1.02)^t$"}]}'::jsonb,103,'{"section_type":"math","sat_domain":"advanced_math","sat_official_domain":"advanced_math","sat_skill":"nonlinear_functions","difficulty":"hard","difficulty_basis":"editorial","content_status":"published","content_revision":"original-2026-10-v2","original_slug":"adv-nlfn-030","answer_format":"mcq"}'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.answer_keys(content_unit_id,correct,metadata) select 'd5f99c7e-a748-b195-e335-5a871736086b','{"option_id":"B"}'::jsonb,'{"feedback":{"explanation":"By the power rule, $(1.02)^{12t} = \\left((1.02)^{12}\\right)^t \\approx (1.268)^t$, so the balance grows by about 26.8% per year. Choice A adds 12 increases of 2% to get 24%, ignoring compounding. Choice D drops the 12 from the exponent. Choice C moves the 12 into the initial amount, which is not a valid rule for exponents."},"source":"original-schood-practice-v2"}'::jsonb where exists(select 1 from public.content_units where id='d5f99c7e-a748-b195-e335-5a871736086b') on conflict do nothing;
